{Cell[
BoxData[{RowBox[{"Print","[","\"Question 3: Both molecules have 9 normal vibrational modes (3N \[Dash] 6 for 5-atom, non-linear molecules). CCl4 has very high symmetry so several vibrations are identical in energy (degeneracies).Although it has 9 modes, it only has 4 peaks. CHCl3 has less symmetry and thus less degeneracies. It has 6 peaks instead of 4.\"","]"}],"\n",RowBox[
{RowBox[{"Print","[","\"Question 4: CHCl3 has a C-H bond which is lighter than C-Cl bonds. When atoms are lighter, frequency increases. \"","]"}],"\n"}]}],
